From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:30:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 26/99] v8: e2k: assemble the LoongArch instructions as e2k
 code

Assembler methods forward to la::Assembler instead of writing loong64
encodings. Labels, relocation and code patching read and write the e2k
slots: branch displacements, the literal of pcaddi and of li64 (one
instruction for any 64-bit constant). Branches reach +-1 GB, so the
trampoline pool is gone. FCSR constants follow %pfpfr.
